2026-03-18T00:09:33 [DEBUG] backend.app.services.resume_parser_service: Parsed resume name='Oli Treadwell  SUMMARYSenior Software Engineer with 10+ years of experience building modern web applicationswith React and TypeScript, plus full-stack delivery with Node.js and Ruby on Rails. Knownfor accessible, user-friendly UI, component-driven architecture (design systems/Storybook),and disciplined testing practices. Hands-on technical leader who mentors engineers throughcomplex work via delegation, code review, and coaching while protecting productionstability. PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCESenior Software Engineer | Numeral Studio | Wellington, NZ | 2025– Present• Delivered reusable React/TypeScript components inside Electron with accessible,responsive UI patterns plus Jest/React Testing Library coverage so compliancereports went in without manual errors.• Built React/TypeScript interfaces and Prisma-backed Node/Express services for secureHR case workflows, adding dynamic staff routing, hardened permissions, andautomated ESLint/Prettier + unit-test checks.• Supported the launch of the design conference 2025 and 2026 site onNext.js/TypeScript with Sanity CMS and Storybook, extending the design system tocut duplicate code and keep the experience polished.• Contributed to a mobile-first interactive marketing demo for a Fortune 500 progressiveweb app, handling localized feature work with remote teams and tuning performancefor fast global launches.• Technologies: React, Next.js, Electron, TypeScript, SCSS, Node.js/Express, PrismaORM, Sanity CMS, Storybook, GSAP, Cypress, Jest, React Testing Library, GitHubActions, ESLint, Prettier, localization & accessibility tools.Software Engineer (Contract) | PartsTrader Markets Ltd. |Wellington, NZ | 2024 – 2025• Developed a dedicated .NET microservice to interface with a legacy API and built amodern, responsive front-end using React with TypeScript.• Translated Figma UI designs into dynamic, accessible interfaces using React,TypeScript, and styled-components.• Applied Domain-Driven Design principles by structuring the microservice withRepository, Domain Model, Mapper, and Application Service patterns.• Technologies: .NET service layer, React, TypeScript, Cypress, GitHub Actions,domain-driven design patterns.' summary_len=268
